## §1 — CL-AUD-021 §3's Y-channel CANNOT-VERIFY, resolved from the jet basis
The missing input is the free-monomial basis. The six pins {f, f_x, f_y, f_xx, f_xy, f_xxx} at the midpoint (the divided-difference image of the pair pins) leave free exactly the jets {f_yy, f_xxy, f_xyy, f_yyy} = (q, a, w, z) at cubic order. Their monomials, with pin-restoring compensation where needed: **q·y²/2 (second order — needs no compensation: value, f_x, f_y all vanish at y=0)**; a·(x²−r²/4)y/2; w·xy²/2; z·y³/6. The q-monomial is *quadratic*, so it enters f at **r²** under y = rY — one order below the cubic monomials' r³. Hence f_y = q·y + O(r²·∂) = r·qY + r²(P_Y − qY) + O(r³), which is CW-DER-008 §2's Y-channel claim. **Third-party corroboration already on the record: GP-PRE-015's field expression contains the raw (Q/2)y² term and the compensated (a/2)(x²−r²/4)y term verbatim** — two models converged on the same compensated field independently. CL is asked to re-verify from this basis; the CANNOT-VERIFY should close or produce a dissent.

